{"id":"NCT04798261","title":"Study of the Long-Term Safety and Outcomes of Treating Pulmonary Embolism With the Indigo Aspiration System","official":"STRIKE-PE: A Prospective, Multicenter Study of the Indigo™ Aspiration System Seeking to Evaluate the Long-Term Safety and Outcomes of Treating Pulmonary Embolism","summary":"The objective of this study is to evaluate real world long-term functional outcomes, safety and performance of the Indigo Aspiration System for the treatment of pulmonary embolism (PE).","conditions":["Pulmonary Embolism"],"interventions":[{"type":"DEVICE","name":"Indigo Aspiration System"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n1. Clinical signs and symptoms consistent with acute PE with duration of 14 days or less\n2. RV/LV ratio ≥ 0.9 assessed by diagnostic computed tomographic angiography (CTA) or echocardiogram\n3. Frontline endovascular treatment with the Indigo Aspiration System per IFU\n4. Patient is ≥ 18 years of age\n5. Informed consent obtained per Institutional Review Board/Ethics Committee requirements\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n1. Contraindication to systemic or therapeutic doses of anticoagulants (e.g. heparin)\n2. Stage IV (metastatic) cancer, active lung cancer or previous history of surgery in the affected lung(s) or chest radiation\n3. Known serious, uncontrolled sensitivity to radiographic agents\n4. Life expectancy \\< 180 days\n5. Patients on ECMO\n6. Pregnant patients\n7. Current participation in another investigational drug or device study that may confound the results of this study. Studies requiring extended follow-up for products that were investigational but have since become commercially available are not considered investigational studies\n8. Other medical, social, or psychological conditions that, in the opinion of the Investigator, precludes the patient from appropriate consent, could limit the patient's ability to participate in the study, including compliance with follow-up requirements, or that could impact the scientific integrity of the study","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":1500,"start":"2021-06-25","pcd":"2026-12","upd":"2026-11-06","sponsor":"Penumbra Inc.","areas":["other"],"central":["Joanne Krasnoff · 650-455-4462 · jkrasnoff@penumbrainc.com","Aisha Pascua · 415-601-9561 · apascua@penumbrainc.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Long Beach Medical Center","city":"Long Beach","pr":"California","zip":"90806","s":"R","lat":33.767,"lon":-118.1892,"c":""},{"f":"Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90048","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":""},{"f":"UCLA Medical Center","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90095","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":""},{"f":"UC Irvine Medical Center","city":"Orange","pr":"California","zip":"92868","s":"R","lat":33.7878,"lon":-117.8531,"c":""},{"f":"UCSD Jacobs","city":"San Diego","pr":"California","zip":"92037","s":"R","lat":32.7157,"lon":-117.1647,"c":""},{"f":"Sharp Memorial Hospital","city":"San Diego","pr":"California","zip":"92123","s":"R","lat":32.7157,"lon":-117.1647,"c":""},{"f":"Christiana Care Hospital","city":"Newark","pr":"Delaware","zip":"19718","s":"R","lat":39.6837,"lon":-75.7497,"c":""},{"f":"MedStar Washington Hospital Center","city":"Washington D.C.","pr":"District of Columbia","zip":"20010","s":"R","lat":38.8951,"lon":-77.0364,"c":""},{"f":"Manatee Memorial Hospital","city":"Bradenton","pr":"Florida","zip":"34205","s":"R","lat":27.4989,"lon":-82.5748,"c":""},{"f":"Blake Medical Center/Nova Clinical Research","city":"Brandenton","pr":"Florida","zip":"34209","s":"R","lat":null,"lon":null,"c":""},{"f":"Delray Medical Center, Inc.","city":"Delray Beach","pr":"Florida","zip":"33484","s":"R","lat":26.4615,"lon":-80.0728,"c":""},{"f":"University of Florida Shands Hospital","city":"Gainesville","pr":"Florida","zip":"32608","s":"R","lat":29.6516,"lon":-82.3248,"c":""},{"f":"Radiology and Imaging Specialists","